% =======================================================
\section{Directional-Sea Stability Target}
\label{sec:sea3-stability-target}

The implementation is intended for oscillatory marine motion, not for an
arbitrary bounded specific-force sequence.  The quantitative source-word proof
of Sec.~\ref{sec:stability-widening-source-path} deliberately remains valid as
the stronger implementation-source envelope, but it can be much more
conservative than the physical deployment class because instantaneous source
bounds alone permit sample-to-sample combinations that no directional sea can
produce.  This section therefore states the stability result that the next
certificate generation is intended to discharge: stability of perturbations of
a physically admissible, oscillatory, multimodal directional sea family.

The result below is a \emph{conditional target theorem}.  Its composition
argument is complete once the listed SEA0/P1--P5 certificates are available,
but this manuscript does not claim a complete SEA0 directional-sea enclosure,
P4 contraction, or the 45-degree SEA3 P5 capture certificate. Conditional
P3 matrix coverage is distinct from these physical and nonlinear obligations.

The primary target is now the bounded-bias motion theorem in
Section~\ref{sec:sea3-bounded-bias-motion}: practical stability of the 18
motion/attitude/gyro-bias errors, with a bounded accelerometer-bias error but
without a claim that this error converges. The estimator still executes its
full active 21-state recursion. The full-state contraction construction and
Theorem~\ref{thm:sea3-regional-practical-stability} below are retained as a
\emph{stronger, unclosed extension}, not prerequisites for the weaker nonlinear
claim. Neither target is closed merely by the bias clamp or by conditional P3.

\subsection{Three-partition directional sea class}

The continuum spectral formulas below describe the retained linear-vessel
branch. The response union in Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-response-union} additionally
admits a correlated atomic Stokes wave-following branch; its bound harmonics
are not identified with this fundamental continuum spectrum.

Fix
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{M_{\max}=3.}
 \label{eq:sea3-mmax}
\end{equation}
For partition $r\in\{1,2,3\}$ let
\begin{equation}
 \lambda_r=(H_r,T_{p,r},\gamma_r,\beta_r,s_r)
 \label{eq:sea3-partition-parameter}
\end{equation}
collect significant-height contribution, peak period, JONSWAP peak-enhancement
factor, mean propagation direction, and directional-spreading parameter.  An
inactive slot is represented by $H_r=0$ rather than by a change of model
dimension.  Under the spectral convention used here, $\gamma_r=1$ gives the
PM limit of the JONSWAP frequency family.

The directional elevation spectrum is
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 E(\omega,\vartheta;\lambda)
 =
 \sum_{r=1}^{3}
 S_J(\omega;H_r,T_{p,r},\gamma_r)
 D_r(\vartheta;\beta_r,s_r,\omega),
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-directional-spectrum}
\end{equation}
where each $D_r$ is nonnegative and normalized over direction.  The partition
energies are coupled by
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{H_s^2=\sum_{r=1}^{3}H_r^2.}
 \label{eq:sea3-total-energy}
\end{equation}
Thus a one-system sea, wind sea plus swell, crossing swell, and a
three-component multimodal sea all belong to one fixed-dimensional parameter
family.  In particular, the proof is not allowed to maximize all three $H_r$
independently while also holding $H_s$ fixed.

The sea parameters evolve through a compact transition relation
\begin{equation}
 \lambda_{k+1}\in\mathcal R_\lambda(\lambda_k),
 \label{eq:sea3-rate-relation}
\end{equation}
whose component bounds include physically justified limits on changes of
$H_r$, $T_{p,r}$, $\gamma_r$, $\beta_r$, and $s_r$.  Those rate limits are
theorem assumptions to be certified by SEA0; they are not fitted to the eight
reference simulations.

\subsection{Directional response and oscillatory source}

On the linear-vessel branch, the spectrum of
Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-directional-spectrum} is not converted to
independent Cartesian acceleration boxes.  Let
$G_{\rm imu}(\omega,\vartheta;\lambda)$ denote the certified directional
sea-to-CoG/IMU response family.  The corresponding matrix-valued source
spectrum is
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \Phi_u(\omega;\lambda)
 =
 \int
 G_{\rm imu}(\omega,\vartheta;\lambda)
 E(\omega,\vartheta;\lambda)
 G_{\rm imu}^{*}(\omega,\vartheta;\lambda)\,d\vartheta .
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-matrix-spectrum}
\end{equation}
It retains the physically coupled cross spectra between the measured vector
components.

For deterministic certification SEA0 supplies an outward enclosure of this
family by an oscillator/shaping state or an equivalent hard finite-window
dynamic constraint,
\begin{align}
 x^s_{k+1}&=A_s(\lambda_k)x^s_k+B_s(\lambda_k)w_k, \nonumber\\
 u^s_k&=C_s(\lambda_k)x^s_k,
 \label{eq:sea3-shaping-system}
\end{align}
with the oscillatory blocks preserving phase continuity.  The compact SEA3
theorem domain includes this deterministic realization coordinate; over a
finite sea window we write it as the coupled history set
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 (x^s_{0:N_W},w_{0:N_W-1})
 \in
 \mathcal X^s_{\rm SEA3}(\lambda_{0:N_W}),
 \qquad
 \mathcal X^s_{\rm SEA3}(\lambda_{0:N_W})\ \text{compact}.
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-hard-realization-set}
\end{equation}
Equation~\eqref{eq:sea3-hard-realization-set} is not an independent disturbance
box and does not reopen SEA3 compactness.  It makes explicit the
phase/driver coordinate already carried by $x^s$ in the complete SEA3 source.
SEA0 must provide a machine-readable outward representation of this coupled
set, its phase-continuous transition, and the left inclusion of the physical
SEA3 realization family into that representation.  The statistical spectrum
of Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-directional-spectrum} constrains the sea family but does
not, by itself, supply a deterministic pathwise bound for
$\mathcal X^s_{\rm SEA3}$.  Consequently, neither a Gaussian confidence event,
spectral moments alone, a replay record, nor a finite seeded harmonic
approximation may replace Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-hard-realization-set} in SEA0/P3.
For SEA3$^+$ this hard-history obligation is imposed branchwise. The Stokes
branch instead uses the nonlinear common-root output below; no linear
$C_s x^s$ identity or continuum quadrature certificate is asserted for it.
Compact source cells at fixed $N$ do not by themselves establish a uniform
cover over the enlarged family.

For an individual undamped oscillator, for example,
\begin{equation}
 \begin{bmatrix}q_{c,k+1}\\q_{s,k+1}\end{bmatrix}
 =
 \begin{bmatrix}
 \cos\omega h&-\sin\omega h\\
 \sin\omega h& \cos\omega h
 \end{bmatrix}
 \begin{bmatrix}q_{c,k}\\q_{s,k}\end{bmatrix}.
 \label{eq:sea3-oscillator-step}
\end{equation}
The actual theorem input is separated as
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{u_k=u^s_k+d^s_k,}
 \label{eq:sea3-perturbed-source}
\end{equation}
where motion generated by admissible changes of the three sea partitions is
part of $u^s$, while $d^s$ denotes bounded out-of-class/model-mismatch input.
The deterministic theorem uses a hard finite-window bound on this input.  A
probabilistic statement for random sea realizations is a later corollary; no
infinite-time pointwise bound is inferred merely from a Gaussian spectrum.

\subsection{Exact tuner reachability and source-language refinement}

The deployed measurement-only adaptation path remains inside the source:
\begin{equation}
 u_k
 \longrightarrow
 \text{WavePeriodEstimator/prior source}
 \longrightarrow
 \text{band variance/EMAs}
 \longrightarrow
 (\tau_k,\sigma_{aw,k},R_{S,k},T_{S,k}),
 \label{eq:sea3-tuner-chain}
\end{equation}
including the exact stage/commit and pseudo-update scheduler state.  Shipping
code uses the fixed $0.2$ Hz tuning prior until the existing
WavePeriodEstimator reports \texttt{hasUsablePeriod()}.  The same estimator
starts its moment statistics after $3/\lambda$, may qualify startup use no
earlier than $4/\lambda$, and additionally requires at least one current
estimated period of moment history.  Its stricter \texttt{isReady()} diagnostic
still requires at least $6/\lambda$ and the existing debiased-moment weight.
The tuner update for sample $k$ executes before the current sample advances the
WavePeriodEstimator, so a newly usable period estimate can affect the tuner no
earlier than the following valid sample.  Filter \texttt{TunerReady} and Live
entry require this startup-usable measured period, but do \emph{not} wait for
\texttt{WavePeriodEstimator::isReady()}.  SEA3/P2 must retain the prior-driven
and startup-usable estimator-driven source modes and their one-sample takeover
edge.

Denote the tuner memory by $z^t_k$ and scheduler/hybrid source memory by $q_k$.
The augmented exogenous state is therefore
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\zeta_k=(x^s_k,\lambda_k,z^t_k,q_k).}
 \label{eq:sea3-augmented-source}
\end{equation}
The SEA3 certificate must establish the sound language inclusions
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathcal L_{\rm actual\ sea}
 \subseteq
 \widehat{\mathcal L}_{\rm SEA3}
 \subseteq
 \mathcal L_{\rm current\ source}.
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-language-inclusions}
\end{equation}
The right-hand language is the existing correlated implementation-source
language; its frozen P2 semantics are not redefined.  Replay records may
falsify either inclusion but may not be used to construct the SEA3 language.

\subsection{Finite sea windows}

With two or three active partitions the modal frequencies need not be
commensurate, so no common wave period is assumed.  Let $T_W$ be a finite
\emph{sea window} and
\begin{equation}
 N_W=\left\lceil T_W/h\right\rceil
 \label{eq:sea3-window-samples}
\end{equation}
its sample count.  SEA0/P3 must choose $T_W$ from a certified
finite-window information condition, not from a replayed trajectory.  A
representative target is
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\mathcal O_{k,N_W}\succeq\alpha_O I,\qquad \alpha_O>0}
 \label{eq:sea3-window-information}
\end{equation}
for every admissible SEA3 window in each fixed-dimensional Live mode.

Let $M(\zeta)\succ0$ be the source-indexed information metric and write
\begin{equation}
 V(e,\zeta)=e^\top M(\zeta)e
 \label{eq:sea3-lifted-energy}
\end{equation}
in local error coordinates, with the exact Cayley lift of
Sec.~\ref{sec:stability-widening-source-path} used for finite attitude error.
The key nonlinear endpoint certificate is the window-wise inequality
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 V_{k+N_W}
 \le
 \rho V_k
 +\gamma_sD_{s,k}
 +\gamma_nD_{n,k},
 \qquad 0<\rho<1,
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-window-dissipation}
\end{equation}
where $D_{s,k}$ and $D_{n,k}$ are hard energies over the window beginning at
$k$.  No one-sample decrease of $V$ is required; growth inside an oscillation
is allowed.

For the homogeneous finite-state part of one complete shipping word, write
$\Phi_N=M_W\Phi_0+d_W$, $J_N=P_N^{-1}$, and
$D_W=J_0-M_W^\top J_N M_W$.  Retain the nonlinear residual, reset, boundary,
and projection history as one same-history coordinate $w_W$, without splitting
it into independent event radii, so that $d_W=B_W w_W$.  Then the exact endpoint
energy difference is the full augmented quadratic form
\begin{equation}
 V_N-V_0
 =
 \begin{bmatrix}\Phi_0\\w_W\end{bmatrix}^{\!\top}
 \underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}
 -D_W & M_W^\top J_NB_W\\
 B_W^\top J_NM_W & B_W^\top J_NB_W
 \end{bmatrix}}_{L_W}
 \begin{bmatrix}\Phi_0\\w_W\end{bmatrix}.
 \label{eq:sea3-joint-word-master}
\end{equation}
If the correlated nonlinear graph is enclosed by quadratic sectors
$z_W^\top\Pi_jz_W\ge0$, $z_W=[\Phi_0^\top,w_W^\top]^\top$, it is sufficient
to find nonnegative multipliers $\lambda_j$ for which the outward full-matrix
test
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{-\left(L_W+\sum_j\lambda_j\Pi_j\right)\succ0}
 \label{eq:sea3-joint-word-sector-test}
\end{equation}
holds.  In active accelerometer-bias mode this test is on the full 21-state
matrix and retains finite-$\tau_b$ bias decay and every state cross term.  Each
suffix in $B_W$ contains every later shipping event, in particular each due
$S=0$ update with the actual applied anisotropic $R_S$.  Thus
Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-joint-word-sector-test} may neither eliminate $a_w$ or
$b_a$ nor replace the same-history graph by a packet-count or independent-box
bound.

The bias source and its initial cell satisfy BIAS0/1 in
Section~\ref{sec:mems-bias-preconditions}.  The full nonlinear graph uses the
corrected error recurrence, not a free GM replacement for $\delta b_a$.
A BIAS2 sector from Eq.~\eqref{eq:bias2-sector} may enter the master only
after its uniform positive separation premise has been verified on this same
graph.  Literature or stationary PSDs cannot supply that certificate.

\paragraph{Source and finite storage attachment.}
Membership of an individual word requires one witness in
Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-hard-realization-set}, its joint translational/rotational
output map, the frontend/tuner root and the BIAS0/1 physical-bias history.
These must generate the word's actual measurements, schedules and $P,H,R$
cells. A capture of those derived cells alone does not supply the missing
witness. The unspecified hard-driver set and joint response realization
must be supplied before this membership predicate is executable; this is
separate from qualifying an assembled accelerometer. Neither declaring a
zero true-bias root after capture nor assigning a SEA3 identifier proves the
same-source equality.

\paragraph{Enlarged response family (SEA3$^+$).}
Retain the entire existing continuum linear-vessel family, with its unchanged
$G\le4$, $f_c\le1.2\,\mathrm{Hz}$, $p\ge2$ envelope, and define
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\mathcal G_{\rm SEA3}^{+}
 =\mathcal G_{\rm vessel}^{\rm linear}
 \cup\mathcal G_{\rm wave\text{-}following}^{\rm Stokes}.}
 \label{eq:sea3-response-union}
\end{equation}
A response-branch label belongs to the source root and is retained through
the entire word and every prefix. This is a union of complete histories, not
permission to switch response laws at individual events. Both branches retain
the same Normal-Live, vector-PE, frontend, tuner, scheduler, zero-lever-arm and
BIAS0/1 premises. Neither branch alone covers the union.

The second branch is the superposition of third-order bound harmonics used
by the wave-following generator, not a claim to solve the full nonlinear
water-wave equations. One lineage fixes a finite number $N$ of atoms,
nonnegative amplitudes $a_i$, directions $d_i=(\cos\vartheta_i,\sin\vartheta_i)$,
root phases $\phi_i$, and fundamental frequencies
$f_i\in[0.02,0.8]\,\mathrm{Hz}$. All directions and phases are admitted;
$N=128$ and seed 42 are one generator instance, not the source quantifier.
Set $\omega_i=2\pi f_i$, $k_i=\omega_i^2/g$, require the model-validity
premise $k_i a_i\le1/5$, and define
\begin{align}
 c_{i1}&=a_i,& c_{i2}&=\tfrac12 k_i a_i^2,&
 c_{i3}&=\tfrac38 k_i^2a_i^3,\nonumber\\
 \theta_i(x,y,t)&=k_i d_i^\top(x,y)-\omega_i t+\phi_i.
 \label{eq:sea3-stokes-root-graph}
\end{align}
The PM/JONSWAP atomic weights and any Stokes variance renormalization are
part of this root, not independently selected harmonic energies. Their
discrete normalization is not the continuum identity
Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-directional-spectrum}. The pinned generator permits a
relative normalization tolerance of $10^{-3}$; use its actual coefficients,
not an assumed exact equality to $H_s^2/16$.

At a fixed material label the centered orbital displacement is
\begin{equation}
 d_o(t)=\sum_{i,n}c_{in}
 \begin{bmatrix}-d_i\cos(n\theta_i)\\\sin(n\theta_i)\end{bmatrix},
 \qquad v_o=\dot d_o,\quad a_o=\ddot d_o.
 \label{eq:sea3-stokes-orbit}
\end{equation}
Use the same atoms to evaluate the surface slopes at the displaced horizontal
point, $s=\sum_{i,n}n k_i c_{in}d_i\cos(n\theta_i)$.
Set pitch $=\arctan(-s_x)$, roll
$=\operatorname{atan2}(s_y,\sqrt{1+s_x^2})$, yaw $=0$, and let $C$ be the
resulting world-to-body rotation. The ideal source outputs are
$f_b=C(a_o-g_w)$ and $\omega_b=\operatorname{vee}(-\dot C C^\top)$.
The pinned implementation approximates $\dot C$ by a centered difference;
its measurement-discretization defect must be bounded and retained, not
silently equated to the exact derivative. Its constant Stokes velocity drift
is separate from centered orbital position and creates no acceleration term.

\paragraph{Branch-specific hard bound.}
For each such root put $B_r=\sum_{i,n}(n\omega_i)^r c_{in}$, $r=0,1,2$.
Then, uniformly over time and every common-root phase/direction,
\begin{equation}
 \|d_o\|\le B_0,\quad \|v_o\|\le B_1,\quad \|a_o\|\le B_2,
 \qquad \|s\|\le\sum_{i,n}n k_i c_{in}.
 \label{eq:sea3-stokes-hard-bound}
\end{equation}
Indeed each trigonometric vector in Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-stokes-orbit} and
its frequency-normalized derivatives has norm one; triangle inequalities
give the first three bounds. The slope bound follows from $\|d_i\|=1$ and
$|\cos|\le1$, also at the displaced point. These are hard model bounds,
not covariance/PSD assertions or P4 nonlinear-remainder budgets. They are
finite for a fixed finite root; a uniform primitive-source cover for all
admitted roots is still an obligation. Normal-Live retention is checked on
the actual joint output; exceeding a conservative $B_2$ bound does not itself
prove violation of the actual acceleration cap.

For a directional Stokes harmonic the
displacement phasor relative to the same elevation harmonic has, up to phase
convention, response $h=(i\cos\vartheta,i\sin\vartheta,1)$ and hence
$\|h\|_2^2=2$. If a third-order generator retains a nonzero harmonic at
$f=3(0.8)=2.4\,\mathrm{Hz}$, the linear-vessel response envelope permits
only $\|h\|_2^2\le[4(1.2/2.4)^2]^2=1$ there. Thus that direct response
witness is outside the linear branch but is no longer excluded from SEA3$^+$:
its higher harmonics belong to Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-stokes-root-graph}. The
linear rolloff moment and surface-period lemmas remain linear-branch results.
The Stokes branch must use its full output moments and exact discrete
frontend history; fundamental surface $T_z$ cannot replace the tuner value.

\paragraph{Certificate composition over the union.}
Let $\mathcal C$ denote the unchanged common Normal-Live/PE, committed
OU/scheduler, process and event premises used by the P3 matrix chain.
For either branch $b$, admissible words lie in $\mathcal W_b\cap\mathcal C$.
The response-independent implication
$\mathcal C\Rightarrow\Omega_W-10^{-18}P_W\succeq0$ therefore applies to
both branches: the H18 prior-free LDLT, the separate H-to-A hybrid direct
sum and later event preservation are rebuilt without changing their margins.
This conditional implication is not a proof that the generator or a retained
word satisfies $\mathcal C$.
P4 must certify Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-joint-word-sector-test}, including BIAS2
when its positive premise is proved, on every source leaf of both branches
and both H18/A21 modes. With a common window and compatible source-indexed
storage, branch bounds combine as $\rho=\max_b\rho_b<1$ and
$\Gamma=\max_{b,j}\Gamma_{b,j}<\infty$, with every-prefix domain retention.
No prefix contraction is required. A missing branch, finite reset/storage
attachment, physical bias root or source cover keeps P4 open and P5 blocked.

For any invertible source-indexed frames $T_j$, a finite change of coordinates
$z_j=T_j e_j$ preserves storage exactly only with the simultaneous transports
\begin{align}
 \widetilde P_j&=T_jP_jT_j^\top,&
 \widetilde f_j(z)&=T_{j+1}f_j(T_j^{-1}z),\nonumber\\
 \widetilde F_j&=T_{j+1}F_jT_j^{-1},&
 \widetilde Q_j&=T_{j+1}Q_jT_{j+1}^\top,\nonumber\\
 \widetilde H_j&=H_jT_j^{-1},&\widetilde R_j&=R_j.
 \label{eq:sea3-finite-storage-pullback}
\end{align}
Indeed, inversion of the covariance congruence gives
$z_j^\top\widetilde P_j^{-1}z_j=e_j^\top P_j^{-1}e_j$,
and substitution gives the finite-map identity. At a pure reset
$P^+=GP_JG^\top$, choosing $T^+=T^-G^{-1}$ removes that covariance
reset in the transformed coordinates. Subsequent prediction, noise, floor
increments, measurement rows and the finite physical map must still undergo
Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-finite-storage-pullback}. Keeping their old numerical
values while deleting resets is generally a different Riccati history.

Equivalently retain the shipping coordinates. For a homogeneous correction,
put $q=e-Ky$, $r=e^+-Gq$, and $b=G^{-1}r$, where $e^+$ is the exact
Cayley/projection output and $G$ uses that correction's own injection. Then
\begin{equation}
 (e^+)^\top(GP_JG^\top)^{-1}e^+
 =q^\top P_J^{-1}q+2q^\top P_J^{-1}b+b^\top P_J^{-1}b.
 \label{eq:sea3-finite-reset-storage-attachment}
\end{equation}
The last two terms remain in the joint nonlinear graph. Their existence is
an exact identity, not a contraction estimate. A zero-error tangent check
does not authorize dropping them or reusing later covariance cells after
changing a finite reset. Until this attachment and source membership hold,
an expanding diagnostic ratio does not falsify the canonical P4 inequality.

Endpoint contraction alone is not sufficient for a full-sample ISS claim.
P4 must additionally certify a uniform prefix-gain inequality: there exist
finite nonnegative constants $\kappa_V,\kappa_s,\kappa_n$ such that for every
admissible SEA3 window and every $0\le\ell<N_W$,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 V_{k+\ell}
 \le
 \kappa_V V_k
 +\kappa_sD_{s,k}
 +\kappa_nD_{n,k}.
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-prefix-gain}
\end{equation}
The full-window energies may be used on the right because they dominate their
prefix restrictions.  This quantitative bound is separate from, and stronger
than, merely proving that all prefixes stay inside the Cayley/source domain.
For a homogeneous prefix $\ell$, the augmented test replaces the upper-left
block $-D_W$ by $M_\ell^\top J_\ell M_\ell-\Gamma_\ell J_0$, with a finite
$\Gamma_\ell\ge1$, and uses only sectors valid for that prefix.  Strict
endpoint contraction does not require prefix contraction.  BIAS1 projection
compatibility and error/source-domain retention must hold at each prefix;
no future-event BIAS2 information may be used to justify an earlier chart.

\subsection{Primary target: bounded bias and practical motion stability}
\label{sec:sea3-bounded-bias-motion}

Write the exact finite error as $(e_H,e_b)$, where
\begin{equation}
 e_H=(c,\delta b_g,\delta v,\delta p,\delta S,\delta a_w)\in\mathbb R^{18},
 \qquad e_b=b_a^{\rm true}-\hat b_a\in\mathbb R^3.
 \label{eq:sea3-motion-coordinates}
\end{equation}
Here $c$ is the finite Cayley coordinate, not a small-angle substitution.
In H18 the estimate is held but the physical bias continues; in A21 both
coordinates follow the full prediction/correction/projection recurrence of
BIAS1. Selectivity of the \emph{storage} does not remove states from the filter.
Choose a same-source storage, in fixed physically scaled coordinates,
\begin{equation}
 W_H(e_H,\zeta)=e_H^\top M_H(\zeta)e_H,\qquad
 m_-\|e_H\|^2\le W_H\le m_+\|e_H\|^2,
 \quad 0<m_-\le m_+<\infty.
 \label{eq:sea3-motion-storage}
\end{equation}
In active mode $\zeta$ retains the complete 21-state nominal/covariance and
bias history. The active gains are not the held-mode gains: for example the
accelerometer gain numerator for $e_H$ contains
$P_{HH}H_H^\top+P_{Hb}$, and its innovation covariance includes the bias
and cross blocks. Thus the H18 certificate cannot be copied to active mode,
nor may a Schur/reduced-state replacement estimator be used.

\begin{lemma}[Conditional compactness of accelerometer-bias error]
\label{lem:sea3-bias-compactness}
Assume the initial estimate lies in the deployed projection ball of radius
$R_b=0.4\,\mathrm{m/s^2}$. Hold, finite-$\tau_b$ prediction with factor in
$(0,1]$, norm-preserving frame changes and the projection after every state
injection preserve $\|\hat b_a\|\le R_b$. If BIAS0/1 additionally supplies a
same-history hard envelope $\|b_a^{\rm true}\|\le B_{\rm true}$, then
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\|e_b\|\le B_e:=B_{\rm true}+R_b.}
 \label{eq:sea3-bias-compact-error}
\end{equation}
No convergence of $e_b$ or identification of $b_a^{\rm true}$ is asserted.
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
Each listed estimate operation preserves the ball, so induction gives the
estimate bound. The triangle inequality gives Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-bias-compact-error}.
The argument does not require true bias to lie inside the projection ball.
\end{proof}
The physical envelope includes uncompensated deterministic offsets and the
BIAS1 driving convolution. A stochastic OU PSD is not a deterministic cap:
a finite-horizon high-probability envelope gives only a correspondingly
conditional finite-horizon conclusion, not an almost-sure infinite-time bound.
Assembled-sensor qualification is required for deployment, not for proving
this conditional implication with symbolic or declared physical bounds.
The estimate bound concerns committed states after the immediate projection;
the pre-projection correction is an auxiliary graph coordinate and need not
lie in the ball.

For this weaker target the old $0.35$ active-estimate interior premise is
replaced by the closed $R_b$ ball; the remaining physical SEA3$^+$, event,
lever-arm and dormant-vibration premises are retained. Consequently all
projection-boundary branches must be covered. An interior-only certificate,
including existing P3 source coverage where it uses that premise, cannot be
silently extended to the boundary. The deployed filter is unchanged.

On a complete word define the \emph{internal coupling energy}
\begin{equation}
 D_{b,k}=\sum_{j=k}^{k+N_W-1}h_j\|e_{b,j}\|^2
 \le T_W B_e^2,\qquad T_W=\sum_{j=k}^{k+N_W-1}h_j.
 \label{eq:sea3-motion-bias-energy}
\end{equation}
Fix $e_{b,j}$ at the sample entrance; every intra-sample bias correction and
projection remains explicitly in the exact joint graph. A certificate must
bound their effect with that convention; it cannot silently sample a different
bias history or drop a correction. $D_b$ is not an exogenous noise budget:
it bounds the actual internal bias-error trajectory, without assuming it is
independent of $e_H$. BIAS0/1 supplies its root/forcing dependence. A BIAS2
sector can sharpen the coupling gain, but positive separation is not required
merely to assert bias compactness; any sector used still needs its own valid
same-history, same-prefix proof.

The new P4-motion obligations, for both response branches and both actual
filter modes, are
\begin{align}
 W_{H,k+N_W}&\le\rho_H W_{H,k}
       +\gamma_bD_{b,k}+\gamma_sD_{s,k}+\gamma_nD_{n,k},
       &&0<\rho_H<1, \label{eq:sea3-motion-endpoint}\\
 W_{H,k;\ell}&\le\Gamma W_{H,k}
       +\kappa_bD_{b,k}+\kappa_sD_{s,k}+\kappa_nD_{n,k},
       &&\ell\in\operatorname{Pref}(W),\quad 1\le\Gamma<\infty.
       \label{eq:sea3-motion-prefix}
\end{align}
All gains are finite and nonnegative. Prefix contraction is not required.
Here $\operatorname{Pref}(W)$ includes every completed shipping event, not
only IMU sample boundaries; each correction includes its immediate reset and
projection, with their auxiliary states retained in the graph.
Every physical model, measurement and gyro-discretization defect stays in its
declared source/noise channel. Removing sensor noise does not set $D_s=0$.
In particular, ocean-wave truth generally does not obey the filter's latent
OU prediction: $x^{\rm true}_{L,j+1}-F_{LL,j}x^{\rm true}_{L,j}$ can remain
nonzero in a noise-free run. Its budget is not removed to obtain contraction.

For a common augmented graph coordinate $z$, write
$e_{H,0}=C_0z$, $e_{H,N}=C_Nz$, and
$D_i=z^\top Q_i z$ for $i\in\{b,s,n\}$. The endpoint master is
\begin{equation}
 L_H=C_N^\top M_{H,N}C_N-\rho_H C_0^\top M_{H,0}C_0
       -\gamma_bQ_b-\gamma_sQ_s-\gamma_nQ_n.
 \label{eq:sea3-motion-master}
\end{equation}
The maps and all dense cross terms come from the same full shipping graph,
including every actual-$R_S$ S event and its finite reset. Valid graph sectors
$z^\top\Pi_jz\ge0$ and $\lambda_j\ge0$ with
$-(L_H+\sum_j\lambda_j\Pi_j)\succ0$ suffice. This is a sufficient augmented
test, not a claim that every sound certificate must be strictly definite in
redundant graph coordinates. Prefix masters replace $C_N,M_{H,N},\rho_H$
by the corresponding prefix maps/metric and $\Gamma$, using only valid prefix
sectors. This changes the performance storage, not the executed covariance.

\begin{theorem}[Regional practical motion stability with compact bias error]
\label{thm:sea3-bounded-bias-motion}
Assume the bias compactness lemma and complete same-history source/event
coverage above, uniform metric bounds, and a finite word length $T_W\le\bar T$.
Retain the canonical P3 matrix checks at $\delta=10^{-18}$, but separately
establish their applicable source premises and the active-mode motion gain;
P3 alone does not prove Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-motion-endpoint}. Suppose P4-motion
proves Eqs.~\eqref{eq:sea3-motion-endpoint}--\eqref{eq:sea3-motion-prefix}
on the relevant first-exit graph and source/noise windows satisfy
$D_s\le\bar D_s$, $D_n\le\bar D_n$. Put
\begin{align}
 C&=\gamma_b\bar T B_e^2+\gamma_s\bar D_s+\gamma_n\bar D_n,\nonumber\\
 C_p&=\kappa_b\bar T B_e^2+\kappa_s\bar D_s+\kappa_n\bar D_n.
 \label{eq:sea3-motion-budgets}
\end{align}
Suppose an endpoint level $L$ and chart-valid level $L_{\rm chart}$ satisfy
\begin{equation}
 W_{H,k_c}\le L,\qquad \rho_H L+C\le L,\qquad
 \Gamma L+C_p<L_{\rm chart}.
 \label{eq:sea3-motion-retention}
\end{equation}
All non-energy source/bias domains are also retained at every subevent.
Then, on successive same-mode complete words after entry,
\begin{align}
 W_{H,k_c+mN_W}&\le\rho_H^m W_{H,k_c}
                   +\frac{1-\rho_H^m}{1-\rho_H}C,\nonumber\\
 \limsup_k W_{H,k}&\le\Gamma\frac{C}{1-\rho_H}+C_p,
 \qquad \|e_{b,k}\|\le B_e.
 \label{eq:sea3-motion-ultimate}
\end{align}
The infinite-time statement requires the envelopes on all successive windows.
A full startup-to-active result additionally requires P5-motion finite capture
and explicit metric/error/source transport at H$\to$A and all other allowed
hybrid events. Capture cannot be inferred from bias compactness.
\end{theorem}
\begin{proof}
The bias lemma bounds each internal coupling energy. Iteration of the endpoint
inequality gives the geometric-series bound. The two level inequalities and
the independently checked source domains exclude a first exit, so the graph
premises remain valid without circularly assuming retention. Apply the prefix
inequality and take the limsup to obtain Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-motion-ultimate}.
Metric coercivity converts this into a motion-error norm bound. A certified
hybrid transport restarts the argument at the next admitted mode level.
\end{proof}

The useful performance quantity is the resulting error floor, in particular
the bias contribution
\[
 \frac{\Gamma\gamma_b\bar T B_e^2}{1-\rho_H}+\kappa_b\bar T B_e^2,
\]
not compactness alone. It must satisfy the desired
motion-accuracy tolerances as well as chart retention. No numerical gain,
accuracy floor, source-uniform motion certificate or bias convergence is
claimed here. P4-motion/P5-motion are separate gates from the retained stronger
full-state P4/P5 gates.
Even with $\bar D_n=0$ and vanishing bias error, nonzero $\bar D_s$ generally
leaves a positive certified upper error floor. The theorem does not require
that floor to be zero, nor does it claim that the upper bound is the attained
error. Observed percentage errors are performance evidence, not numerical
theorem constants until the relevant output normalization, source family and
gain bound have been certified.

\subsection{Stronger full-state conditional stability theorem}

\begin{theorem}[Three-mode directional-sea regional practical stability and
finite capture]
\label{thm:sea3-regional-practical-stability}
Assume the following hold uniformly for both fixed-dimensional Normal-Live
modes and both response branches of Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-response-union}.

\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*),leftmargin=2.1em]
\item BIAS0 qualifies the sensor model and its residual/mismatch envelopes;
BIAS1 attaches the true bias and corrected-error history to the source,
including projection compatibility and physical continuation through hold and
H$\to$A.  Stochastic and calibration/model mismatch contributions remain
in the declared forcing energies.
\item SEA0 supplies a sound outward enclosure of the complete response union.
On the linear branch this is the three-partition directional sea class of
Eqs.~\eqref{eq:sea3-directional-spectrum}--
\eqref{eq:sea3-shaping-system}, including the compact hard realization set of
Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-hard-realization-set}, its declared rate-bounded parameter
evolution, and its directional vessel/IMU response. On the Stokes branch it
is the joint root graph of Eqs.~\eqref{eq:sea3-stokes-root-graph}--
\eqref{eq:sea3-stokes-hard-bound}, including physical IMU discretization
defects where applicable. Neither enclosure replaces the other.
\item P1 places the execution in the declared Normal-Live operating branch,
including the current no-accelerometer-rejection condition and the declared
startup prior/estimator source split.
\item P2 proves Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-language-inclusions} while preserving the
exact deployed period-source mode, tuner, parameter-EMA, stage/commit, and
pseudo-update scheduler history.
\item P3 supplies bounded positive source metrics and a strict finite-window
linear information/contraction margin on every SEA3-complete window.
Its configured finite-$\tau_b$ matrices are retained at $\delta=10^{-18}$.
Any later change to those matrices requires a new quantitative P3 build;
qualification alone does not change the deployed time constant or process $Q$.
\item P4 verifies both Eqs.~\eqref{eq:sea3-window-dissipation} and
\eqref{eq:sea3-prefix-gain} for the exact nonlinear shipping word map on an
invariant inner funnel $\mathcal F_{\rm inner}$, with every prefix inside its
declared chart/source domain.
Any BIAS2 sector it consumes has a certified positive constant on the exact
same-history nonlinear graph, as required by Theorem~\ref{thm:bias2-separation}.
\item P5 proves that every admitted 45-degree entrance state reaches
$\mathcal F_{\rm inner}$ in at most $K_{\rm cap}$ samples while respecting the
hybrid obligations.
\end{enumerate}

Then for the capture time $k_c$ and every integer $m\ge0$,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 V_{k_c+mN_W}
 \le
 \rho^mV_{k_c}
 +
 \sum_{j=0}^{m-1}
 \rho^{m-1-j}
 \left(
 \gamma_sD_{s,k_c+jN_W}
 +\gamma_nD_{n,k_c+jN_W}
 \right).
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-practical-iss-sum}
\end{equation}
For every $0\le\ell<N_W$, combining this endpoint estimate with
Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-prefix-gain} gives the explicit intermediate-sample bound
\begin{align}
 V_{k_c+mN_W+\ell}
 &\le
 \kappa_V\rho^mV_{k_c} \nonumber\\
 &\quad +\kappa_V
 \sum_{j=0}^{m-1}
 \rho^{m-1-j}
 \left(
 \gamma_sD_{s,k_c+jN_W}
 +\gamma_nD_{n,k_c+jN_W}
 \right) \nonumber\\
 &\quad +\kappa_sD_{s,k_c+mN_W}
 +\kappa_nD_{n,k_c+mN_W}.
 \label{eq:sea3-practical-iss-prefix}
\end{align}
If every post-capture sea window satisfies
$D_{s,k_c+jN_W}\le\overline D_s$ and
$D_{n,k_c+jN_W}\le\overline D_n$, then
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \limsup_{m\to\infty}V_{k_c+mN_W}
 \le
 \frac{\gamma_s\overline D_s+\gamma_n\overline D_n}{1-\rho}.
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-practical-ultimate}
\end{equation}
and Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-practical-iss-prefix} yields the full-sample bound
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \limsup_{k\to\infty}V_k
 \le
 \kappa_V
 \frac{\gamma_s\overline D_s+\gamma_n\overline D_n}{1-\rho}
 +\kappa_s\overline D_s+\kappa_n\overline D_n.
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-practical-ultimate-full}
\end{equation}
Uniform upper/lower bounds on $M(\zeta)$ then convert these energy inequalities
to a regional practical ISS bound on the error norm.  When both perturbation
energies vanish, the inner error converges exponentially at sea-window
endpoints and Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-prefix-gain} carries that convergence between
endpoints.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
P5 gives a finite $k_c$ with the state in the P4 invariant funnel.
Equation~\eqref{eq:sea3-window-dissipation} can then be iterated on consecutive
SEA3-complete windows because P2/SEA0 preserve source completeness and P4
preserves the funnel.  Iteration gives
Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-practical-iss-sum} with disturbance energies indexed at the
actual post-capture window starts.  Applying the certified prefix inequality to
the window beginning at $k_c+mN_W$ gives
Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-practical-iss-prefix}.  Bounded disturbance energies and the
geometric series give Eqs.~\eqref{eq:sea3-practical-ultimate} and
\eqref{eq:sea3-practical-ultimate-full}; uniform metric equivalence then gives
the corresponding error-norm statement.
\end{proof}

The theorem is called \emph{regional} because the present entrance set is
fixed at 45 degrees.  A semiglobal corollary would require the certificate
construction to succeed for every prescribed compact entrance subset of the
Cayley chart; that stronger claim is not assumed here.

\subsection{Shipping envelope used by the new certificate}

The SEA3 construction must use the current deployed clamps rather than the
historical wider proof envelope.  The source at this revision gives
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{@{}ll@{}}
\toprule
Quantity & Current bound\\
\midrule
tuning frequency & $0.03\le f_{\rm tune}\le1.2$ Hz\\
OU time constant & $0.02\le\tau\le12$ s\\
OU acceleration standard deviation & $\sigma_{aw}\le4$ m/s$^2$\\
$R_S$ scalar clamp & $0.15\le R_S\le100$\\
$S=0$ pseudo-update period & $0.005\le T_S\le0.150$ s\\
dynamic EMA horizon & $\le35$ s\\
Normal-Live accelerometer rejection & not admitted\\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
These are source-parity values, not fitted sea parameters.
